{"abstract":"We present a separation logic specification and verification of linked lists with views, a data structure from the C5 collection library for .NET. A view is a generalization of the well-known concept of an iterator. Linked lists with views form an interesting case study for verification since they allow mutation through multiple, possibly overlapping, views of the same underlying list. For modularity, we build on a fragment of higher-order separation logic and use abstract predicates to give a specification with respect to which clients can be proved correct. We introduce a novel mathematical model of lists with views, and formulate succinct modular abstract specifications of the operations on the data structure. To show that the concrete implementation realizes the specification, we use fractional permissions in a novel way to capture the sharing of data between views and their underlying list. We conclude by suggesting directions for future research that arose from conducting this case study.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Jonas Braband","Birkedal, Lars","Sestoft, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384820"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Formal verification","Modularity","Separation logic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modular verification of linked lists with views via separation logic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5381/jot.2011.10.1.a2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384820","identifier":[{"id":"79952849992","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f17e55b0-7342-4890-9cd6-51aa408af784"],"keyword":["Separation logic","formal verification","modularity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4224B0F4E517C28DAEE072AE418E265A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5381/jot.2011.10.1.a2","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Braband","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jonas Braband","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","name":"Birkedal, Lars","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"sestoftpau","last":"Sestoft","locid":"0ee7ba1e-3108-4db3-a908-97977980d032","name":"Sestoft, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-5843-6021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5381/jot.2011.10.1.a2","issn":["16601769"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Object Technology","pages":"21-40","publisher":"Journal of Object Technology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Object Technology","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952849992"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f17e55b0-7342-4890-9cd6-51aa408af784"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modular Verification of Linked Lists with Views via Separation Logic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384820","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Research relies on ever larger amounts of data from experiments, automated production equipment, questionnaries, times series such as weather records, and so on. A major task in science is to combine, process and analyse such data to obtain evidence of patterns and correlations. Most research data are on digital form, which in principle ensures easy processing and analysis, easy long-term preservation, and easy reuse in future research, perhaps in entirely unanticipated ways. However, in practice, obstacles such as incompatible or undocumented data formats, poor data quality and lack of familiarity with current technology prevent researchers from making full use of available data. This paper argues that relational databases are excellent tools for veterinary research and animal production; provides a small example to introduce basic database concepts; and points out some concerns that must be addressed when organizing data for research purposes.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sestoft, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384091"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animal Production Research","Data management","Data quality","Relational Databases","Research Data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organizing research data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:10.1186/1751-0147-53-S1-S","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384091","identifier":[{"id":"84855288983","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c1709072-c491-4132-960b-10f65a6b4d78"],"keyword":["Animal Production Research","Data Management","Data Quality","Relational Databases","Research Data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-BDB82027F7A70DDACCDBF8A86696DD30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.actavetscand.com/content/pdf/1751-0147-53-S1-S2.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:10.1186/1751-0147-53-S1-S","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"sestoftpau","last":"Sestoft","locid":"0ee7ba1e-3108-4db3-a908-97977980d032","name":"Sestoft, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-5843-6021","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1751-0147-53-s1-s","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"issue":"S2","journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","title_org":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica (Print)","volume":"55, suppl 1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855288983"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1709072-c491-4132-960b-10f65a6b4d78"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Organizing research data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384091","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
